CONVERT
  - takes character in A (in EBCDIC)
  - converts to Forth character in A

ACCEPT
  - if at the end of the current record, load new record
  - fetches a character from record
  - converts to Forth char

RETRV
  - gets character at *2 address C
  - stores into A

NEXT
  - put two blanks in WORD+1
  - accept a character
  - if it's 0-20 is alpha
  - if it's 21-22 is SPEC1
  - if it's not 25 is SPEC1
  - deposit into W
  - TODO??

W1 - *2 address of word buffer

ALPHA
  ?

FETCH
  - takes a *2 address in ACC
  - loads a character 8-bit into A

C1 - RESET CHAR ?
C2 - Char beyond record?
C3 - Char beyond sector?

DEPOSIT
  - takes an *2 address in ACC
  - takes character in A
  - stores to a character to *2 addr
  - for even characters only seems to clip to 6-bits ?
  - for even characters only adds in 0x24 (BL)

PUT
  - takes Forth char in A
  - converts to BCD via table
  - stores it into PRN at DP, increments DP
  - calls PRINT if DP == DP1
  - restores Forth char in A

DP0
DP  - *2 ptr into PRN 74 char buffer
DP1

PRINT
  - calls PRNT1 to print whole buffer if full
  - seems to call DEPOSIT with A if not until full
  - note this would not convert to EBCDIC
